The Library of the World (corona): the memory of the Narrator, a horizontal zen-cybernetic cloister with an open court, a dark water mirror and the runes of the canon.
Written by Gemini CLI (Gemini 3.8 Flash, subscription) on 23/10/2026, task T19.
Box: 14 × 14 × 7 tiles, 112 × 112 × 56 voxels, 8 voxels per tile.
Key letters:
  O = door (letter O, name "porta", at the centre x=56, y=102, z=0..19, inner hall empty and open through to the court)
  F = sign ("BIBLIOTECA DEL MONDO", green neon 7dd87d with a steady glow on a plate above the door)
  P = dark matte plate for the sign
  M = primary cybernetic black metal (1×1 pillars, lintels, court frame and blade roof)
  m = dark secondary metal (panelling, posts, pool kerbs)
  C = graphite concrete (perimeter base, ambulatory, parvis and walkway)
  S = light steel (finishes of the roof blade, collars and lantern spire)
  s = dark steel (transition kerbs and joints)
  V = dark reflecting glass
  v = bands of cold ash-blue reflection
  W = dark mirroring water of the court (10202a)
  N = bright green accent neon (7dd87d glow)
  n = soft green neon for the threads at the base of the pillars (4a984a glow)
  x = temporary buffer for the animation (hidden)
Pulsing phases of the canon (1..8):
  1..8 = continuous gradient of 8 phases (from 489848 to 7dd87d with glow) for the meditative breathing of the runes and the lantern.
Architecture:
  A low, horizontal building (12 × 12 tiles, ~3 tiles high, z=0..25) with a flat, thin, jutting blade roof.
  A continuous outer portico with very close black pillars (1 × 1 voxel, every 5 voxels) with a green neon thread at the base.
  Recessed walls in dark reflecting glass with posts and bands of reflection.
  An inner court open to the sky (6 × 6 tiles = 48 × 48 voxels, x=32..80, y=32..80) with a flush dark water mirror (W, z=1).
  On the surface of the water (z=1), flush, the 8 runes of the canon lit in geometric green in a sacred symmetric composition.
  A single tall, thin zenith lantern (z=0..48, ~6 tiles) in the north-east corner of the water mirror, with a light on top.
  Door O centred to the south at z=0 with a wide gap in the colonnade and an inner hall open through to the court.
  The sign "BIBLIOTECA DEL MONDO" on two lines centred on the edge of the roof above the door.
Animation "canone" (8 frames):
  A fluid, cyclic breathing of the light of the runes immersed in the water mirror and of the top core of the lantern.
-->
